    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44782" root="&#xA;                        ويل&#xA;                    " body-key="w1">
                        
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَيْهًا</span></b> 
                         [an imperative verbal noun, which may
be rendered <i>On!</i>] a word of incitement. (S, K.)
One also says to a man, and to a horse, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَا وَيْهَاهْ</span>
[<i>Ho! On!</i>]. (A'Obeyd in TA in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ايه</span>.) See
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَيَّهَ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَيْهَكَ</span>: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَيْهَكَ</span> in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ايه</span>. I have not
found this anywhere but in that art. in the K,
and doubt its correctness.

